+# No Entry Point to the Specialty Directory
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+The specialty directory (REQ-SPEC-001) inverts the veterinarian directory: it lists each specialty with the veterinarians holding it. REQ-SYS-001 states that every page carries navigation to the owner and veterinarian areas. A new page normally earns a place in that navigation, so its absence would read as an oversight rather than a decision.
+
+The product owner settled the question at intake on 2026-08-08: "The page is reachable by its URL alone: no navigation entry and no link from another page is part of this request. A visible entry point may come as a follow-up request."
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Add a navigation entry beside the veterinarian directory.** Rejected: it was not requested, and it would widen REQ-SYS-001's navigation contract in the same slice that introduces the page.
+2. **Link the specialty directory from the veterinarian directory.** Rejected for the same reason, and it would couple two pages the owner scoped independently.
+3. **Ship the page reachable by its address alone** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+The specialty directory has no navigation entry and no inbound link. It is reached by entering its address. Recorded as NG-10.
+
+The page still carries the standard navigation to the owner and veterinarian areas, so REQ-SYS-001 continues to hold on it unchanged.
+
+A visible entry point is a follow-up request, not a deferred part of this one. Adding one narrows NG-10 and needs its own recorded owner decision.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The page is discoverable only to a reader who knows its address. That is the intended reach for now.
+- REQ-SPEC-001 carries an acceptance bullet asserting that no page links to the directory, so an incidental link fails the suite.
+- NG-2 is untouched: the directory reads specialties and veterinarians, and manages neither.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-10
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the NG-10 row.
+- [PRD REQ-SPEC-001](../prd.md#req-spec-001) — the requirement whose reach this decision bounds.
