+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-spec-001"></a>
+
+The clinic also publishes the inverse of the veterinarian directory. It lists every specialty the clinic knows, each by its stored name, with the veterinarians holding it. A veterinarian is shown by first name then last name. A specialty no veterinarian holds still appears, with none listed under it. A veterinarian holding no specialty appears nowhere: the page lists specialties, not the whole roster. Every specialty is shown on the one page, which is reached by its own address rather than from a link `[REQ-SPEC-001]`.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-SPEC-001]` given the specialties the clinic knows, when the specialty directory is opened, then every one is listed by its stored name.
+- `[REQ-SPEC-001]` given a specialty two veterinarians hold, when the directory is opened, then both are listed under it by first name and last name.
+- `[REQ-SPEC-001]` given a specialty no veterinarian holds, when the directory is opened, then it is listed with no veterinarian under it.
+- `[REQ-SPEC-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian appears nowhere on the page.
+- `[REQ-SPEC-001]` given more specialties than one screen holds, when the directory is opened, then all are on the one page and no paging control is offered.
+- `[REQ-SPEC-001]` given every page of the system, when each is rendered, then none links to the specialty directory.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A clinic that knows no specialty renders an empty directory rather than failing.
+2. Specialties, and the veterinarians under each, are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
+3. A specialty name is shown as stored. It is not translated with the page's surrounding wording.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts) · **ADR:** [ADR: No Entry Point to the Specialty Directory](adr/2026-08-08-non-goal-specialty-directory-entry-point.md)
+
